# dalivim-runner deploy config.
#   cp deploy/runner.env.example deploy/runner.env   # runner.env is gitignored
# Only non-secret tuning lives here. The service token is managed by deploy.sh
# (reused from the live container or generated, stored in deploy/.runner-token).
# Every value below is a default baked into deploy.sh — uncomment only to change one.

# --- image & container name ---
# IMAGE=dalivim-runner
# CONTAINER=runner

# --- fail-closed hardening (do not relax in prod) ---
# RUNNER_SANDBOX=require              # boot fails if the nsjail cell can't engage
# RUNNER_NETWORK_ISOLATION=require    # boot fails if per-run netns can't be created
# RUNNER_CGROUP=require               # per-run cgroup memory accounting (R6).
#                                     # Use 'auto' until './deploy.sh setup' has made
#                                     # the delegated cgroup reboot-safe, else a reboot
#                                     # downs the runner (fail-closed on a missing cgroup).
# RUNNER_CGROUP_MOUNT=/sys/fs/cgroup/dalivim

# --- R6 cgroup placement. Requires the cgroupfs docker driver (see deploy.sh setup). ---
# CGROUP_PARENT=/dalivim              # empty string disables R6 placement entirely

# --- per-run limits (empty => the image's built-in defaults: 128 / 512 MB) ---
# RUNNER_DEFAULT_MEMORY_MB=128
# RUNNER_MAX_MEMORY_MB=512

# --- outer container budget (separate from the per-run caps) ---
# CPUS=1
# MEMORY=1g
# PIDS_LIMIT=512
# NPROC=512

# --- pin the token explicitly (optional). Normally leave unset and let deploy.sh
#     manage deploy/.runner-token. Set this only to force a specific secret. ---
# RUNNER_SERVICE_TOKEN=
